<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 100.00 from 99.75, the Bundesbank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The move, effective immediately, brings the yield on the Series 123, 4.50 percent paper down to 4.50 percent from 4.55 percent.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
